With --split-mode tensor a model's weights loaded far slower than split by
layer, also after 0010 gathered the rows (Qwen3-235B Q4_K_M over four MI250X
GCDs 352 s cold against 113 s by layer, Qwen3-Coder-480B over eight 569 s
against 113, c11-placement load-*, 20-10-2026). The meta buffer has no
events or host buffers, so the loader gave it no async uploads from pinned
memory: each weight read into memory was read whole, then copied, the file
idle during the copy and the devices idle during the read; the meta buffer
copied it to its devices one after the other from one thread; and both the
buffer each weight was read into and the one its rows were gathered in were
allocated anew for every weight. Reading into pages never touched before ran
at a fifth of the speed of reading into pages already touched (0.33-0.49
against 2.6-2.9 GB/s, 512 MiB pieces from memory), and on LUMI-G the reading
was most of the load: 221-272 s of Qwen3-235B's, the copying 26-53 s
(next22, 22-10-2026).

Now, for a meta buffer, the loader reads the next weight while the last one
is copied (LLAMA_LOAD_OVERLAP=0 reads and copies in turn) and logs how long
reading, copying and waiting took; the weights are read into the same buffers
one after the other, two at most, allocated at the size of the largest. The
meta buffer copies a weight of 16 MiB or more to each device on a thread of
its own (GGML_META_SET_THREADS=0 copies one device after the other) and
gathers rows into buffers kept from call to call, one for each thread
gathering at once.

With the buffers reused, copying Qwen3-235B to its GCDs took 13-21 s instead
of 26-53, but reading it still 209-253 s, against 130 s for the whole load
split by layer (next23, 22-10-2026): each weight was read with one read of
hundreds of MiB, where layer split reads 1 MiB at a time with the file
system's read-ahead running ahead of it. Each weight of a meta buffer is
now read by 16 threads at once, in positioned reads of 16 MiB
(LLAMA_LOAD_READ_THREADS; 1 reads it with one read, as before). With 1, 8
and 16 threads (next24, 22-10-2026) Qwen3-235B as two servers of four GCDs
loaded in 248, 206 and 140 s (124 by layer), Qwen3-Coder-480B over eight in
275, 160 and 121 s (162 by layer), gpt-oss-120b as four servers of two in
120, 83 and 59 s (69 by layer).

Since upstream #31321 (29-10-2026) the loader's own staging read reuses its
buffer and reads direct-IO files without a bounce buffer; a buffer that is
not a meta buffer, or LLAMA_LOAD_OVERLAP=0, goes that way, timed for the log
line above.

